<<^ code=`&#x0002;`>>

```toml meta
cacheable = true
l-space   = "stable"
role      = "settle a standoff with both: records take the file, drafts stay"
tags      = ["lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/affordance", "lar:///carriage.disk.merges"]
title     = "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/afford/carriage.disk.merges"
type      = "text/memetic-wikitext+tiddlywiki"
uri-path  = "ha.ka.ba/lares/afford/carriage.disk.merges"
```

<<~ ahu slot=`#/head`>>

! carriage.disk.merges ~ a person keeps the file's words as parallel drafts and the records' render on disk

`keep-both <uri> key=<key>` writes the records' render over the file and keeps the file's words as parallel drafts in the worn face's draft layer. It appears in the standoff alert where drafts stand; `drafts <uri>` names them by title, and `lares get` reads each. SETTLING STAYS A HAND ACT: an AI harness on its branch refuses `hand-act-only`, an unreadable branch `hand-unattested`, and `yes=true` approves nothing by itself.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/shows`>>

!! shows ~ keep-both

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`example` name=`keep-both` params=`uri/lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/example key/<key> ~ the records' render lands on disk and the file's words stay as drafts`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/takes`>>

!! takes ~ uri · key · bag · yes

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`arg` name=`uri` params=`takes/lar-address needs/required seat/1 as/<uri> ~ the carrier at the standoff`>>
<<has entity=`arg` name=`key` params=`takes/key needs/required ~ the standoff's key, as lares shore printed it`>>
<<has entity=`arg` name=`bag` params=`takes/bag-uri ~ the bag that holds the carrier`>>
<<has entity=`arg` name=`yes` params=`~ name the intent for a call off a terminal; approves nothing by itself`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/gate`>>

!! gate ~ hand-act

Testimony: the door checks; this slot grants nothing.

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`gate` name=`hand-act` params=`who/hand ~ a settling act reads the hand behind this command before anything else; an AI harness on its branch refuses hand-act-only, an unreadable branch hand-unattested, each naming the command the operator runs, and yes=true approves nothing by itself`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/refuses`>>

!! refuses ~ hand-act-only · usage · a-state-that-moved

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`refusal` name=`hand-act-only` params=`cure/[[carriage.disk.reads]] ~ an AI harness settles nothing; the line names the command the operator runs`>>
<<has entity=`refusal` name=`usage` params=`cure/[[carriage.disk.merges uri/<uri> key/<key>]] ~ a carrier and the standoff's key both stand required`>>
<<has entity=`refusal` name=`a-state-that-moved` params=`~ an answer names the state its giver read (a standoff's key, or the count that stands pending); where that state moved, the island refuses by name and nothing changes`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/answers`>>

!! answers ~ took · aborted

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`band` name=`took` params=`exit/0 ~ the records' render landed and the drafts stayed`>>
<<has entity=`band` name=`aborted` params=`exit/1 ~ the person answered no at the prompt`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/skins`>>

!! skins ~ cli

<<~ ahu slot=`#/skins/cli`>>

!!! lares shore keep-both

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`skin` name=`cli` params=`handler/host spells/[[lares shore keep-both]] ~ the terminal; settling stays a hand act`>>
```

